is executed only by separately opted-in, hash-checked diagnostics.

## SigLIP image encoder provenance

The official Sarashina model card identifies the image encoder's base model as
Google SigLIP SO400M patch14-384:
https://huggingface.co/google/siglip-so400m-patch14-384

The SigLIP model card states Apache-2.0, and the original big_vision repository
also states that its models are released under Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/google-research/big_vision/blob/0127fb6b337ee2a27bf4e54dea79cff176527356/README.md#license

See [LICENSE.siglip](LICENSE.siglip) for the complete Apache-2.0 text, obtained
from that big_vision revision. This identifies the source of the license text,
not the big_vision revision used to train Sarashina. No separate upstream NOTICE
file was found in the inspected SigLIP HF file list or that big_vision tree.
This is a downstream attribution notice, not an upstream NOTICE file.

## Changes made by Jev Local

- Converted the official checkpoint's image encoder, merger and final LayerNorm
  to GGUF using Jev Local's conversion script; no additional training.
- Included `mm.post_norm.weight` and `mm.post_norm.bias`, which were missing
  from the previously distributed projector conversion.
- Recorded the vision FFN width as 4304 and used the project-specific
  `sarashina2vl` projector type; the result contains 442 tensors.
- Recorded `jev.sarashina.preprocess_version=1`, the official image-area limits,
  and official source/configuration hashes. The matching runtime normalizes
  before float bicubic resize instead of using the legacy Pillow uint8 path.
- The GGUF contains F16 multidimensional weights and F32 one-dimensional
  parameters. The binary's description also identifies the included final
  LayerNorm and the need for the updated Jev Local runtime.

Conversion and compatible runtime source: Jev Local commit
`5edbee00dcdd01690cbbd9cd1dd4d8f300862cd0`:
https://github.com/Argos1111/jev_local/tree/5edbee00dcdd01690cbbd9cd1dd4d8f300862cd0

The conversion script is `scripts/convert_sarashina_mmproj.py`. These runtime
sources include `native/sarashina-official-preprocess-b11042.patch`; the older
cf973239 commit does not implement this preprocessing version. Prebuilt runtime:
https://github.com/Argos1111/jev_local/releases/tag/sarashina-llama-b11042-pre1

The required runtime separately corrects image boundaries, preprocessing and
normalization. Its source/patches are available in Jev Local; no runtime binary
or language-model GGUF is included in this projector-only distribution.

mradermacher is the distributor of the compatible language-model GGUFs and the
original projector used for comparison. The corrected projector here was
converted directly from the official checkpoint, not from mradermacher's
projector file. The existing mradermacher language GGUFs are unchanged; observed
tokenization differences from the official tokenizer remain a separate issue.

This is an independent, unofficial derivative. No endorsement by SB Intuitions,
Google or the llama.cpp project is implied. The model's known limitations and
validation scope are documented in the
[Jev Local Sarashina notes](https://github.com/Argos1111/jev_local/blob/5edbee00dcdd01690cbbd9cd1dd4d8f300862cd0/docs/SARASHINA.md).
